# Telegram bots for the BBS bridge. Copy this file to .env, next to
# docker-compose.yaml, and fill it in. .env is gitignored: never commit or
# print it. Without TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN the bridge is off and the BBS runs as before.
#
# The code reads only TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN: the token of the bot this machine
# runs, from @BotFather. Use a separate TEST bot on a development machine.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
#
# The PRODUCTION bot's token, kept here only to copy it into the production
# machine's .env as TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN. Never run two BBS instances with one
# token: both poll Telegram, conflict (409) and split the updates between them.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN_PROD=
